# ⚠ This used to be `/norebo`, meant for the built binary. On case-insensitive
# file systems (the macOS default) that line also swallows the `Norebo/`
# directory with the language library: git compares names case-insensitively
# when core.ignoreCase is on. The library silently stayed out of the
# repository, and the Oberon environment image was built without it.
#
# The same trap is already described in the Makefile, where it made the
# `norebo` target collide with the directory. Now we write the binary's name
# exactly as it is actually produced.
/norebo.bin

# Intermediate bootstrap stages. ⚠ build2 is NOT listed here: it is the base
# the compiler runs on and goes into the environment image (see NOREBO_PATH).
/build1/
/build3/
